669:
No cellar or basement space shall be used as a habitable room or dwelling unit unless:
(1) Floors, walls. The floors and walls are impervious to leakage of underground and surface runoff water and are insulated against dampness;
(2) Minimum window area. The total of window area in each room is equal to at least the minimum window area sizes as required in section 12-128 of this article;
(3) Location of window area. Such required minimum window area is located entirely above the grade of the ground adjoining such window area; and
(4) Openable window area. The total of openable window area in each room is equal to at least the minimum as required under section 12-129 of this article, except where there is supplied some other device affording adequate ventilation and approved by the building official.
(Code 1968, § 14-32)

778:
Every pawnbroker shall maintain a book, in permanent form, in which shall be entered in legible English at the time of each loan, purchase or sale:
(1) The date of transaction;
(2) The name of the person conducting the transaction;
(3) The name, age and address of the customer; a description of the general appearance of the customer; and the distinctive number from the customer's driver's license or other similar identification card; the identification used must contain a photo of customer;
(4) An identification and description of the pledged or purchased goods, including, if reasonable available, the serial, model or other number, and all identifying marks inscribed thereon;
(5) The number of the receipt or pawn ticket;
(6) The price paid or the amount loaned;
(7) The number of the check issued for the purchase price or loan if payment is made by check;
(8) The maturity date of the transaction; and
(9) The signature of the customer.
(10) It will be the duty of the owner or employees to have the customer hold the number of their receipt in front of their chest and a color photo made. The photo supplies/equipment will be purchased by the licensee and preserved and furnished to the police for development/processing at the city's expense of the city sees the necessity.
(Ord. of 2-24-78, § 15-67; Ord. (W-4-93) of 3-2-93; Ord. (W-26-07) of 3-6-07)
State Law reference— Similar provisions, Ga. Code Ann., § 44-12-132.

796:
Every dealer in gold, silver or precious metals shall maintain a book in permanent form in which shall be entered in legible English at the time of each transaction or purchase a record thereof which shall contain the following information:
